// Package shopee — Shopee device-risk telemetry payload.
//
// This blob is a static device fingerprint captured from one real browser
// session. The passport web client's fraud SDK posts it to the device-risk
// report endpoint before any OTP request. Without it (or an equivalent report
// the issuer recognises), Shopee reports OTP success but silently suppresses
// delivery of the code.
//
// Understand the trade-off before using this constant:
//
//  1. It is a *shared* fingerprint. Every installation that passes it reports
//     the same device to Shopee, so accounts become linkable to each other and
//     to the capture device.
//  2. If Shopee flags this fingerprint, it stops working for everyone at once.
//  3. Supplying a report that does not describe the machine actually making the
//     request is, in substance, working around an anti-fraud control and may
//     breach Shopee's terms.
//
// Prefer the honest alternative: capture your own report from your own browser
// and pass it as ProviderConfig.DeviceReport.
//
// This constant is exported for parity with the reference implementation, not
// because replaying it is recommended.
package shopee

// DeviceRiskBlob is the reference device-risk report that yields a full-strength
// risk token. Prefer supplying your own DeviceReport instead.
const DeviceRiskBlob = ``
